From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:37:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] selftests: apple-dcp: stub the m4 panel VRR request
 in the VRR unit

"drm/apple: m4: adaptive sync on the J604 panel, as an experiment" makes
the m4 branch of dcp_crtc_atomic_check() call
iomfb_m4_panel_vrr_requested(), which the vrr-rejection host unit does
not declare, so the unit no longer compiles.

Stub it like the other m4 helpers of this unit: iomfb_is_m4() is false
here, so the m4 branch must never be reached and the stub asserts.

[j604: integration fix for the optional DCP vrr + boost side branch of
 linux-aurora 1.608, on top of the main-line stub for
 iomfb_m4_atomic_check_hdr(). No kernel code change.]

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/lifecycle.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/lifecycle.py b/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/lifecycle.py
index 7292941555..5e12168e97 100644
--- a/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/lifecycle.py
+++ b/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/lifecycle.py
@@ -1803,6 +1803,8 @@ static int iomfb_m4_get_mode(struct apple_dcp *d,struct drm_display_mode *m)
 static int iomfb_m4_atomic_check_hdr(struct apple_dcp *d, struct drm_crtc *c,
     struct drm_atomic_commit *s)
 { (void)d; (void)c; (void)s; assert(false); return -ENODEV; }
+static bool iomfb_m4_panel_vrr_requested(struct apple_dcp *d)
+{ (void)d; assert(false); return false; }
 static unsigned drm_plane_mask(void *p) { (void)p; assert(false); return 0; }
 static bool drm_mode_equal(const struct drm_display_mode *a,const struct drm_display_mode *b)
 { (void)a; (void)b; assert(false); return false; }
